 ### R2-Gaussian Training Paradigm
-A volume reconstruction method trained primarily from X-ray projections, using volumetric data only as a regularization signal, optimized to match projection consistency rather than direct volumetric fidelity [S2, unofficial]. It synthesizes X-ray projections from ground-truth volume using TIGRE toolbox, provides both synthetic projections and ground-truth volume to R2-Gaussian during reconstruction, and optimizes network to match X-ray projections [S2, unofficial]. It achieves higher 2D PSNR than volumetric methods because it is optimized for projection matching, but yields significantly lower 3D PSNR (e.g., 22.92 vs 51.54 on Aneurysm) due to lower 3D spatial fidelity [S2, unofficial]. Training time is notably faster [S2, unofficial]. Due to lack of support for large raw volumetric data, comparisons are limited to datasets up to the Neuron size [S2, unofficial].
+A volume reconstruction method trained primarily from X-ray projections, using volumetric data only as a regularization signal, optimized to match projection consistency rather than direct volumetric fidelity [S2, unofficial]. It synthesizes X-ray projections from ground-truth volume using TIGRE toolbox, provides both synthetic projections and ground-truth volume to R2-Gaussian during reconstruction, and optimizes network to match X-ray projections [S2, unofficial]. It achieves higher 2D PSNR than volumetric methods because it is optimized for projection matching, but yields significantly lower 3D PSNR (e.g., 22.92 vs 51.54 on Aneurysm) due to lower 3D spatial fidelity [S2, unofficial]. R2-Gaussian demonstrates notably faster training times compared to AVIS [S2, unofficial]. Due to lack of support for large raw volumetric data, comparisons are limited to datasets up to the Neuron size [S2, unofficial].
 
 ## Operating characteristics
-- **Time Complexity:** Not given in the sources. Training time is notably faster than some volumetric methods for R2-Gaussian, but AVIS training time depends on the number of iterations and densification steps [S2, unofficial][S1, unofficial].
